# Client Requirements — Kamogelo Insurance Brokers

Source: approved project brief, CMPG325-2026-089, Client CLI-089.

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| Assigned organisation | Kamogelo Insurance Brokers (Vryburg) |
| Industry | Professional Services |
| Assigned addressing block | 192.168.40.0/24 (single block, subnetted internally via VLSM) |
| Connectivity & services | Provide appropriate connectivity and network services for the assigned scenario |
| Design constraint | Boardroom requires dedicated wired and wireless presentation ports |
| Change request (CR15) | A second Internet connection is added for resilience and must be integrated |
| Assigned networking challenge | Wireless LAN (AP integration & coverage) — Foundational difficulty |
| Deliverable | A working, testable Cisco Packet Tracer implementation |

## Interpretation Notes

The brief specifies requirements and constraints but not internal department
structure. The following organisational assumption was made to translate a
generic "Professional Services" brokerage into concrete network segments:

- A small insurance brokerage of this type is assumed to consist of four
  functional areas: **Sales/Brokers** (largest headcount — client-facing
  policy sales), **Admin & Management** (reception, admin support,
  management), a **Boardroom** (client meetings and presentations — the
  segment named directly in the design constraint), and a small
  **Server/Infrastructure** segment for shared resources.
- This assumption drives the VLAN structure documented in
  `../02-network-design/`. It does not add scope beyond the brief — it only
  operationalises "Professional Services" into segments a real Vryburg
  brokerage would plausibly have. This should be confirmed against the CMPG
  325 Project Handbook or lecturer guidance if it conflicts with common
  project conventions.
